WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.820
Satellite images of the North Carolina
coastline reveal features in the landscape

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.590
scientists cannot explain.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:15.540
The shapes are large and oval or egg shaped
and stretch for miles and miles.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.630
They're everywhere, one after another after
another.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.530
It's got to be the biggest mystery in all of
American geology.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:29.500
George Howard is investigating the mysterious
structures nicknamed the Carolina Bays.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.440
These are amazing features.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.490
I don't know what they are.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.480
They're low and flat and circled with a
white bay rim.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.020
It's absolutely amazing.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.560
Recent satellite images have only added to
the mystery.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.830
These things are present in huge numbers.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:49.010
People think that there might be half 1000000
to 2 million of them.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:53.360
Despite their nickname, the Bays are not
confined to North Carolina.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.150
Strange enough to see him in one location.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:01:00.380
But what's crazy is when you zoom out, you
can see that they extend from Florida all the

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.600
way up the Eastern seaboard to Delaware.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.060
You can live on them. People's houses are all
over them.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.170
Highways go through them.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.640
Their shopping centers around them.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.910
George Howard is out searching for one of the
shapes.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.360
It's more difficult than it looks.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.810
This appears to be a white sandy rim here of
a bay.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.800
It curves both sides to the left and the
right.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:29.540
You can only see them when you're flying
overhead and that's when you get a real good

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.550
look at the strange pattern on the ground.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:36.650
George is using a drone to analyze the
structure of the elliptical shapes.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:42.560
To be able to get out here and actually use
some of this amazing technology to fly.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.010
Basically robotic aerial cameras above
Carolina Bay.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.360
It is really special.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:56.540
Once airborne, the drone's camera helps to
locate his position in the egg shaped bay.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.950
Wow. We are definitely where we thought we'd
be looking at the photography.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:02.840
I think we're right on it right now.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:07.340
We can see the interior choked with
vegetation in here and just a beautiful,

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.940
brilliant white sand defining the western
edge of the bay.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.490
It's not just the existence of these egg
shapes that baffle scientists.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.750
It's also the strange alignment.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.550
What's so crazy about this is that they're
all stretched in the same way.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:26.060
So it looks like someone took all these
circles and just kind of dragged them so that

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.610
they're all slanted in one particular way.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.320
What's odd about this?

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:35.720
What's really bizarre is how do you get
ovals in the same shape and in the same

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.600
orientation as really strange?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:43.130
Some experts think a clue may lie in the age
of the bays.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:47.540
These shapes were created during the last
Ice Age thousands of years ago.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.370
It's a time when.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.570
North America was a very different place.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:59.020
It's a time when ice sheets were creeping
down from the north, upwards of 10,000 feet

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:04.960
thick ice sheets that are equivalent to what
we would find today in Antarctica.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:11.230
In this strange world of ice, prehistoric
humans lived alongside many creatures that

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.540
have long since disappeared from the earth.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.490
Right before the end of the Ice Age.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.770
There were amazing mammals that walked
through this very area mastodons, mammoths,

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:25.510
saber toothed tigers, beavers, the size of
VW bugs.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:31.720
Some scientists speculate if these enormous
egg shapes are the work of giant beavers.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.000
These beavers were like no beavers we have
today.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:40.030
They were massive, probably had incisors 6
to 12 inches long, just a whole nother scale

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.360
of beaver and not something you would want
to run into out here today.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:48.580
But even giant beavers would have difficulty
building dams on this scale.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.420
I'm kind of amazed that the animals are
capable of building such uniform structures

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.280
all in the same orientation.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.720
They all talking to each other.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:04.210
It would take a lot of giant beavers to make
this many structures.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:07.780
Where are all their bones instead of
beavers?

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:13.440
Some scientists have linked the egg shapes
to a terrifying Ice Age apocalypse.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:19.600
One theory about the Carolina Bays is that
some kind of an impact hit the ice sheet and

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.750
actually blew chunks of ice down into lower
latitudes.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:30.550
Giant ice bombs the size of massive icebergs
crashing down from the skies.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.980
The thought is as terrifying as it is
bizarre.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:39.070
You can only imagine if icebergs were
launched hundreds of miles from the glacial

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.220
ice sheet at hypersonic speeds.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:45.820
They would have landed in this landscape and
it exploded with the force of many, many

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:46.870
atomic bombs.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:51.490
But how could super massive ice bombs have
created the pattern we see today?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.630
Maybe this is what happened.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.730
If you were standing here during this event,
there would have been absolutely nothing you

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.960
could have done. You could run a mile in any
direction and you'd be still walking your way

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.100
into apocalypse.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.780
The animals would have been wiped out.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.520
But not everyone accepts the giant ice bomb
theory.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:19.630
There's nothing that big that's going to hit
a sheet of ice and send giant ice cubes

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:24.640
soaring through the sky to land on the
ground hundreds of miles away to form an

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.560
impact crater. It just doesn't work.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.040
Scientists are still unable to explain these
images.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:35.830
We don't know why these shapes are here, why
they are this shape, why they are aligned in

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.130
this strange way.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.930
We don't know what or who made them.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:45.190
It's just so fascinating that there are still
things on earth, even something as abundant

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:49.000
and widespread as this that we just don't
have an answer to.

